ong one directed edge. After you move to a destination, the opponent acts from that destination. If that destination has no outgoing edges, the opponent loses. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N0\n\nDirected graph:\nN6 -> N7\nN3 -> N6, N9\nN9: no outgoing edges\nN2: no outgoing edges\nN4 -> N8, N7\nN0 -> N6, N1\nN1 -> N3, N5\nN8: no outgoing edges\nN7: no outgoing edges\nN5 -> N4, N2\n\nLegal moves: N6, N1assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N0, the legal moves are to N6 or N1. Evaluating each move:\n\nOption 1: Move to N6\nFrom N6, the next move options are to N7 (N7 has no outgoing edge → opponent loses immediately after N6 → N7; thus, N6 is a winning move)\n\nOption 2: Move to N1\nFrom N1, options go to N3 and N5:\n- N3 leads to N6/N9 (N9 is terminal → opponent will be forced into losing path after N3→N6→N7 or N3→N9)\n- N5 leads to N4/N2; N4 leads to N8 or N7, both dead ends; N2 leads to terminal (dead end at N2 → opponent moves into losing state)\n\nThus, all paths through N1 lead to branching where opponent eventually hits a sink node, and player gains control via forced endgame.\n\nHowever, the key insight: From N0 → move directly to N6 → opponent reaches N7 and cannot move further; opponent loses. This is immediate win.\n\nN6 → N7: opponent now at N7 has no outgoing edge → opponent cannot move → loses.\n\nThus, move to N6 is optimal, immediately forcing opponent to lose.\n\nFinal move: N6</reason>\n<answer>N6</answer>", "episode_score": -0.95, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N0, the legal moves are to N6 or N1. Evaluating each move:\n\nOption 1: Move to N6\nFrom N6, the next move options are to N7 (N7 has no outgoing edge → opponent loses immediatel