[2026-08-19 09:33:51] [agentic_pipeline.py (561)] [INFO] [DRIVER 0 / 1][PID 2147319] [{"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. After you move to a destination, the opponent acts from that destination. If that destination has no outgoing edges, the opponent loses. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N9\n\nDirected graph:\nN9 -> N6, N5\nN13 -> N0, N12\nN12 -> N10, N4\nN5 -> N2, N8\nN1: no outgoing edges\nN7: no outgoing edges\nN4: no outgoing edges\nN6 -> N3, N7\nN0: no outgoing edges\nN10: no outgoing edges\nN2 -> N13, N3\nN8 -> N4, N11\nN11 -> N10, N1\nN3: no outgoing edges\n\nLegal moves: N6, N5assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N9, you must move. Evaluate all moves to maximize outcome.  \n- Move to N6:  \n  - Opponent chooses N3 or N7 (N3 ends game, N7 is terminal).  \n  - If opponent chooses N3 (terminal), opponent loses, you win.  \n  - If opponent takes N7 (terminal), opponent loses, you win.  \n  - So all outcomes lead to opponent losing immediately.  \n- Move to N5:  \n  - Opponent chooses N2 or N8.  \n  - Opposite to N2: opponent returns to N13 → N0 or N12.  \n  - N13 → N0 or N12 → N10 or N4.  \n  - N10 or N4 are terminal nodes.  \n  - N8 → N4 (terminal) or N11 → N10 or N1 (terminal).  \n  - So opponent can eventually trap or lead to opponent losing.  \n  But under N6, direct terminality is secured.  \n  N6 → N3 or N7 both terminal. So opponent loses immediately.  \n  N5 leads into longer chain but still terminal.  \n  However, N6 offers direct terminal response.  \n  Since both moves lead to opponent losing eventually, but N6 has immediate terminal opt